From 847793929684e7d70694abfcaab6fd82025c1cf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:49:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(templates): generated apps depend on the merged
 framework only (B7)

The templates still wrote @strutvane/core, @strutvane/cli and the
strutvane launcher into every new app, next to @strutvane/framework,
which now contains core and the CLI (framework CONSOLIDATION.md). A new
app therefore had two kernels (container tokens and error classes from
two copies) and three packages declaring the strutvane / strutvane-cli
bins, so which CLI `npm run dev` or `npm run sv` ran depended on npm's
link order.

- dependencies: @strutvane/framework for every preset (ui peer-depends
  on it too); no @strutvane/core
- devDependencies: no @strutvane/cli, no strutvane launcher
- `sv` runs `strutvane` (the framework bin); README text updated
- generated code imports @strutvane/framework/core
- generated engines.node and this package's engines: >=24.3
- the bin drift check resolves the framework through node_modules
  instead of a sibling ../cli checkout, so it no longer skips silently
  in per-repo CI (B5)
- new test: per preset, no absorbed package and no launcher
- goldens regenerated (vitest -u)

The generated-project type-check needs @strutvane/framework 0.1.0-next.1
(devDependency); apply after it is published and regenerate the lockfile.
B8 (the installer itself still depends on @strutvane/devkit) is a
separate decision and is not changed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
